    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="0122" n="110" xml:id="pg110"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/67<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >5/24</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in El Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gade</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-11T17:00:00-06:00">September 11, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. For General Strong. Permission granted by Salvadoran Government for
                    photographic air mission to operate in this country based on San Salvador.
                    Strongly urge that both Honduran and Salvadoran aviators be given some
                    instruction in methods and equipment used. Mathewson.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
